--- !u!114 &-7143992264150807267
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "The <b>Sky</b> is set up using the <i>Lighting</i> window.\n\n1. Head to <b>Window</b> > <b>Rendering</b> > <b>Lighting</b>\n\n2. At the top of the <i>Lighting</i> window, select the <i>Environment</i> tab.\n\n3. In the <i>Environment</i> foldout, a <b>Skybox Material</b> is required for the sky to render.\n\n4. Double-click on the Skybox Material <b>GardenSkybox_Mat</b>\n\n5. In the <i>Inspector,</i> experiment with the <b>Tint Color,</b> <b>Exposure</b> and <b>Rotation</b> properties.\n\n\n<b>Important</b> \n\nThe Skybox will influence the ambient lighting and reflections in the Scene: its influence is controlled with the <b>Environment Lighting</b> and <b>Environment Reflections</b> properties. \n\nIf your changes are not immediately visible in the Scene, you may need to click on the <i>Generate Lighting</i> button at the bottom of the <i>Lighting</i> window to update the lighting. This process may take several minutes."
