  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'In this tutorial, you learned how the Sky and Fog are set up.


      For more information, you can check out the href="https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/sky.html"<a>documentation.</a>


      <b>Note:</b> You do not need to save your changes in order to follow other tutorials.'
--- !u!114 &5220784908725275792
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'Similarly to the Sky, the <b>Fog</b> is set up using the <i>Lighting</i> window.


      1. Head to <b>Window</b> > <b>Rendering</b> > <b>Lighting</b>


      2. At the top of the <i>Lighting</i> window, select the <i>Environment</i> tab.


      3. In the <i>Other Settings</i> foldout, toggle the <b>Fog</b>  on and off. This may require shaders to be compiled.


      4. Experiment with the <b>Color,</b> and distance at which the Fog will <b>Start</b> and <b>End,</b> to better understand how the fog interacts with the environment.


      5. Undo your changes'
